// A pose must also SAY where it is: {} and {"orientation":[0,0,0]} both decode
// to the origin, which is a real place in the cell and one nobody means. An
// absent ORIENTATION is left at zero — that is the wire format's own convention
// for "no rotation" and callers rely on it — but an absent position is not a
// convention, it is an omission, and this format exists so a point states where
// it is.
