## Not in the spec

The former v2 shape could say a few things the spec cannot. They are still
**read** and honored, but have no wire form, so a re-emitted document loses
them (the dataset service stores documents verbatim, so nothing stored is
rewritten):

| former v2 | in the spec |
|---|---|
| `parameters` (declared holes) and their command `id`s | none; callers can still fill holes on plan/execute/session-create for documents that declare them |
| `start: {type: point}` | only `start_joint_position`; a start from a stored point is decoded, not re-emitted |
| `tool.offset` (flange→TCP offset at teach time; "tool changed since teaching" check) | `tcp` only; planning uses the description's current offset |
| `frame: {type: dataset_frame, frame, dataset}` (cross-dataset frame) | a bare frame id; the graph follows from context |
| `revision` pin on a point target | none (spec gap S2); `source_revision` is the snapshot's revision, not a pin |
| closed target / command shapes | the spec's objects are open |

Each of these is a candidate follow-up to the teaching spec.

## The dataset service (2026-09-08)

